--TEST--
A `catch` binding answers through properties, so every PHP accessor is refused where it is written — spec § 10, `rule:errors/propagation`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:errors/properties-not-accessors
// Spec § 10 gives the exception tree `message`, `previous`, `backtrace` and
// `location`, and `nvs_types::error_lib` seeds exactly those plus the
// synthesized constructor. A ported program writes PHP's accessors on
// purpose, so each is the ordinary unknown-member refusal with a help naming
// the property that answers the same question — never a panic below the
// checker.
try {
    throw new LogicError("boom");
} catch (Throwable $e) {
    echo $e->getMessage(), "\n";
    echo $e->getPrevious(), "\n";
    echo $e->getTraceAsString(), "\n";
    // `getFile` and `getLine` are one property here: a throw site is one
    // string.
    echo $e->getFile(), "\n";
    // `getCode` is the accessor with no counterpart at all — `rule:errors/propagation`
    // propagates a class, never a number — so it names the whole roster
    // instead of one property.
    echo $e->getCode(), "\n";
}

// The subclass spelling is the same rule: the refusal is keyed on the
// exception tree, not on the root.
try {
    throw new LogicError("again");
} catch (LogicError $e2) {
    echo $e2->getMessage(), "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0405]: `Throwable` has no method named `getMessage`
%A
   = help: the exception tree declares properties rather than accessors — write `->message`; spec § 10 lists `message`, `previous`, `backtrace`, `location`
%A
error[E0405]: `Throwable` has no method named `getPrevious`
%A
   = help: the exception tree declares properties rather than accessors — write `->previous`; spec § 10 lists `message`, `previous`, `backtrace`, `location`
%A
error[E0405]: `Throwable` has no method named `getTraceAsString`
%A
   = help: the exception tree declares properties rather than accessors — write `->backtrace`; spec § 10 lists `message`, `previous`, `backtrace`, `location`
%A
error[E0405]: `Throwable` has no method named `getFile`
%A
   = help: the exception tree declares properties rather than accessors — write `->location`; spec § 10 lists `message`, `previous`, `backtrace`, `location`
%A
error[E0405]: `Throwable` has no method named `getCode`
%A
   = help: the exception tree declares `message`, `previous`, `backtrace`, `location` and no method but its constructor
%A
error[E0405]: `LogicError` has no method named `getMessage`
%A
error: aborting due to 6 errors
